All —

Quick heads-up while I've still got a minute at the desk. We had a bus-vs-pole and bus-vs-pedestrian collision on S. Main just north of Third at approximately 02:05 this morning (10/18/2025). Operator is R. Keeler, badge 4417, running Owl service. RPD is on scene, EMS transported the pedestrian (critical), and two aboard were injured. Keeler is with RPD; roadside PBT came back over the limit per the officer on scene. Bus is 4177 — being held for the DOT post-accident testing per Part 655.

Here's the thing I want to flag before it drops off my radar: pulling it up on the dispatch console just now, Keeler appears to have been running off-book / not on his assigned route tonight. The pin at the time of the call doesn't match where I'd expect a 512 bus to be at 02:0X, and I don't see a matching timepoint on my board. I could be reading the screen wrong at this hour — it's been a night — but it looked off to me and I want it in writing before end of shift.

I'll pull the block sheet in the morning to confirm one way or the other and follow up. If it turns out he was off-book that obviously changes the picture for the safety write-up and for whatever Risk needs to do, so I didn't want to sit on it.

Marlene — sending to you directly so you have it before you come in. Happy to walk through what I saw on the console when you're in.

More to come once I've had coffee and the daylight version of the schedule in front of me.

— Wes

